# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-cad-quit-saves-modified-drawing -- an unattended alfe run ended the CAD with QUIT Y: a modified drawing was saved, or the CAD sat on a save prompt
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-cad-quit-unsaved
#+DATE: 2026-10-23

* Symptom

pjb, 2026-10-23: after the dxf-angles probe (MR !472), AutoCAD on the
Windows runner PF5S26B stayed open on "dxf-angles-probe.dxf", stuck.

* Cause

The CAD-side runtime ends an unattended session (*AUTOLISP_QUIT_ON_FINISH*,
on for every non-interactive AutoCAD / BricsCAD run) with
(command "_QUIT" "_Y"), and a failed bootstrap with the same: QUIT's "Save
changes?" answered YES. A drawing the run modified is then SAVED -- under
the name the run last gave it (the probe's COM SaveAs had renamed the
document to dxf-angles-probe.dxf) or, for an unnamed drawing, through the
Save As dialog when FILEDIA is 1 -- a modal dialog nobody answers on an
unattended runner. alfe's own COM quit (quit-autocad.vbs) closes documents
WITHOUT saving, but only for an instance this run created, and the runtime's
QUIT comes first.

* Fix (2026-10-23, clautolisp 2.3.44 / alfe 2.3.44)

- autolisp-bootstrap.lsp: AUTOLISP-HOST-QUIT sets FILEDIA 0 and issues
  (command "_.QUIT") when DBMOD is 0, (command "_.QUIT" "_N") -- discard --
  when the drawing is modified; the repl loop's final quit uses it; the
  fatal bootstrap path does the same inline (it may run before the
  function is defined).
- The dxf-angles probe leaves its document UNMODIFIED: it exports to a work
  file (never the artefact), copies the export aside as measured, restores
  its sysvars, then saves the document through COM if DBMOD is set, and
  reports DBMOD before / after (INFO DBMOD-at-end). On accoreconsole
  (DXFANG_BACKEND) it skips COM, which ended the run there
  (dxf-angles-probe-accoreconsole-export).
- Not changed: the accoreconsole SCR's ._QSAVE / ._QUIT _Y (headless, a
  deliberate save of the drawing it was given, no dialog possible); alfe's
  attach-to-a-running-AutoCAD behaviour (runs in its active document and
  quits nothing it did not create) -- see the question below.
- Test PROTOCOL-EMITTED-RUNTIME-QUITS-WITHOUT-SAVING: no QUIT in the
  emitted runtime answers Yes, the bootstrap's is DBMOD-guarded; red (3
  checks) against 2.3.43's runtime, green now.

* To close

Run dxf-angles:probe:autocad:windows and :accoreconsole:windows on the MR;
check INFO DBMOD-at-end 0 in the reports and that no AutoCAD is left open
on the runner (pjb's eye on PF5S26B, or the next job's CAD sweep).

* Open question (pjb)

When alfe ATTACHES to an AutoCAD that is already running, it runs in that
instance's ACTIVE document (adding one only when none is open) and quits /
closes nothing afterwards. A run that renames or modifies the active
document (as a SaveAs does) changes whatever drawing was active -- possibly
a person's. Should an attached run work in a document of its own, and
close it (without saving) at the end?

* Verified on the runners (2026-10-23, MR !474) -- DONE

dxf-angles probe on 2.3.44 (pipeline 2980965341): AutoCAD 2022 GUI (job
17414697753) ended its run with the drawing still MODIFIED -- INFO
DBMOD-before-final-save 4, DBMOD-at-end 4: AutoCAD's COM Save from inside
the running LISP did not clear the "system variable modified" bit -- i.e.
exactly the state in which the old QUIT _Y saved and hung. With 2.3.44's
DBMOD-guarded QUIT _N the session ended: pjb checked PF5S26B afterwards, no
AutoCAD left open. BricsCAD V25 Windows (17414697752) and V26 macOS
(17414697751): DBMOD 5 -> 0 after the probe's own save, clean exit.

pjb also found a suspended alfe.exe-old* process on the runner (left over
from the earlier stuck run, presumably) and terminated it: see
alfe-windows-old-exe-left-suspended.

The open question on ATTACHED AutoCADs (runs in the active document,
closes nothing) stays open; it is a design decision for pjb, not part of
this fix.
